bug_report:
assert() in multiversioned functions causes compilation error
As the bug title says:

#include <stdio.h>
#include <assert.h>

__attribute__((target("default")))
void foo(int x)
{
        assert(x >= 0);
}

__attribute__((target("arch=haswell")))
void foo(int x)
{
        assert(x >= 0);
}

When compiled:

/tmp/ccCQK5gF.s: Assembler messages:
/tmp/ccCQK5gF.s:71: Error: symbol `_ZZ3fooiE19__PRETTY_FUNCTION__' is already defined
